\pard\sb0\sa180\f0\fs48\b\cf1 Ledgerly\b0\par
\pard\sa300\f0\fs22\cf2 Installation and User Guide | 11 November 2026\par
\pard\sa180\f0\fs22\b\cf3 Keep the complete Ledgerly App folder together. Your Excel workbook and business records are not included.\b0\par
\pard\sb240\sa100\f0\fs30\b\cf1 1. Package contents\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 business-ledger.html is the application. ledgerly-icon.svg and ledgerly-icon.ico are the browser and Windows shortcut icons. start-ledgerly-sync.cmd and ledgerly-sync.ps1 are the local Windows Excel connector. Documentation contains the draft User Terms and Conditions.\par
\pard\sb240\sa100\f0\fs30\b\cf1 2. Install on another Windows device\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 1. Copy the entire Ledgerly App folder to a permanent location on the other computer, such as Documents. Keep the HTML, icon, CMD and PowerShell files together.\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 2. Open business-ledger.html in Microsoft Edge or Google Chrome. The app needs no installer or internet connection. Excel synchronization requires Windows and desktop Microsoft Excel.\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 3. To transfer records, open Ledgerly on the old device and use Documents & reports > Export data. Copy the JSON backup securely to the new device. In Ledgerly on the new device choose Import backup and select that JSON file. Import replaces records on the new device, so export its current records first if you need to keep them.\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 4. Records are stored in the browser profile on each device, not in the application folder or in a cloud account. The new device has separate browser data until you import a backup. Keep using the same browser profile and export a backup before moving or renaming the app.\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 5. For a taskbar shortcut, create a shortcut that opens business-ledger.html in Edge or Chrome. In shortcut Properties > Change Icon, select the included ledgerly-icon.ico, then pin the shortcut.\par
\pard\sb240\sa100\f0\fs30\b\cf1 3. Save and protect records\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 Click Save on each form. Saved entries remain in that browser on that device after closing the app or restarting Windows. Unfinished forms are not saved.\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 Use Documents & reports > Export data regularly and store the JSON backup somewhere safe, preferably on a separate drive. Do not clear the browser profile or site data used by Ledgerly. The app does not automatically upload records to the cloud.\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 CSV and print/Save as PDF options are available for one account or all transactions, one item or all inventory, one batch or all production, one trip or all transport records, and all opening/account balances. Use the record selectors in each section. Exports and printouts include relevant entered details and calculated inventory/production costs. JSON is the recommended complete app backup for transferring records.\par
\pard\sb240\sa100\f0\fs30\b\cf1 4. Everyday use\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 Overview shows sales, gross profit, expenses, net profit or loss, the current cash/bank balance carried down, and recent transactions. The greeting follows Kenya local time (East Africa Time), not the computer's configured time zone.\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 In Documents & reports, choose Set opening balances. Enter the date the balances apply from, then add Cash & M-Pesa, Bank, each customer who owes you, each supplier you owe, each loan account and each capital account with its balance. Account names must match the names used in later transactions. The report shows balance b/d (brought down), movements, and balance c/d (carried down). Activity dated on or after the selected date updates those balances.\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 Transactions record sales, purchases, other income and operating expenses. Enter the customer for sales and supplier for purchases. Stock transactions require quantity and unit price. Use Customer receipt to reduce a debtor, Supplier payment to reduce a creditor, Loan received / Loan repayment to update a named loan, and Capital introduced / Capital withdrawal to update a named capital account. These account movements affect balances and cash/bank, not profit and loss; record loan interest separately as an expense. On the Transactions page, choose an Account / description to download or print those records separately, or download or print all transactions. Stock records are grouped by item name.\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 Inventory stores stock items and opening quantity/cost. Leave opening cost blank only when genuinely unknown; the app marks that stock uncosted. Use the inventory selector to download or print one item's stock and valuation details, or choose all inventory.\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 Production records the finished item and output quantity, each raw material and quantity, additional production costs, payment method and notes. Production uses available costed material stock. Material and additional costs become finished-goods inventory cost and are recognized in profit and loss as goods are sold. Use the production selector to download or print a batch costing sheet, or choose all batches.\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 Transport & export records the load, carrier, departure and arrival, mileage, fuel, additional costs, payment and load value. Load value is a dispatch memo, not income. Download or print an individual trip using its selector; the all-trips CSV and print ledger contain the recorded trip details.\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 Documents & reports can print transaction documents, production batch sheets, dispatch notes and profit-and-loss reports. Choose Save as PDF in the print dialog to keep a PDF.\par
\pard\sb240\sa100\f0\fs30\b\cf1 5. Separate company profiles\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 Use the Company switcher in the sidebar to add another company or switch between companies. Existing Ledgerly data is kept as the first company when this version opens. Each profile has separate business details, transactions, inventory, production, transport, opening balances and Excel sync history. A new company starts with an empty ledger and inventory. Switching companies does not change the other company's records.\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 Company profiles are local records in the same browser profile, not separate logins or password-protected user accounts. Use Export data separately for each selected company. Backups and Excel workbooks should also be kept separate.\par
\pard\sb240\sa100\f0\fs30\b\cf1 6. Optional two-way Excel synchronization\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 Excel workbook paths are stored separately for each company. In Sync Excel, assign each company a different full Windows path ending in .xlsx. The suggested path is beside the Ledgerly App folder. The workbook is not included; copy it separately to the target device, or select Create the workbook if this file does not exist to make a new one. Never assign the same workbook to two companies.\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 1. Save your workbook edits and make a separate workbook backup. Open it in desktop Excel with editing enabled. 2. Double-click start-ledgerly-sync.cmd and keep its PowerShell window open. Copy the one-time token shown. 3. In Ledgerly, select the company, click Sync Excel, confirm its workbook path, paste the token and select Read, merge & sync. Resolve any conflicts by choosing which version to keep. 4. The connector writes to LEDGERLY INVENTORY, LEDGERLY TRANSACTIONS, LEDGERLY TRANSPORT, LEDGERLY PRODUCTION and LEDGERLY OPENING BALANCES tabs; original workbook tabs are preserved. Close the connector when done.\par
\pard\sa180\f0\fs22\b\cf3 Excel synchronization is manual, not continuous. Save workbook edits before syncing. Do not sync the same workbook from multiple computers at once.\b0\par
\pard\sb240\sa100\f0\fs30\b\cf1 7. Important limitations\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\cf0 Ledgerly is a lightweight recordkeeping tool, not a bank feed, cloud synchronization service, tax filing system or substitute for professional accounting advice. Reports depend on the dates, quantities and costs entered. Review totals and retain source receipts and invoices.\par
}